Here is an experimental CSS setup that explores various shades of lime and green using blend modes, layered gradients, and shade ramps:

```css
/* ============ Lime & Green Shade Experiment ============ */

:root {
  /* Green → lime shade ramp */
  --green-900: #052e16;
  --green-700: #15803d;
  --green-500: #22c55e;
  --lime-400:  #a3e635;
  --lime-300:  #bef264;
  --lime-200:  #d9f99d;
}

/* Base: deep green canvas */
body {
  background-color: var(--green-900);
  color: var(--lime-200);
  font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
}

/* Hero: lime background, green text, inverted shading */
.hero {
  background: linear-gradient(
    135deg,
    var(--lime-300) 0%,
    var(--lime-400) 45%,
    var(--green-500) 100%
  );
  color: var(--green-900);
  padding: 4rem 2rem;
}

/* Experimental: layered radial "shade orbs" */
.orb-field {
  background-color: var(--green-700);
  background-image:
    radial-gradient(circle at 20% 30%, var(--lime-400) 0%, transparent 25%),
    radial-gradient(circle at 70% 60%, var(--green-500) 0%, transparent 35%),
    radial-gradient(circle at 50% 90%, var(--lime-200) 0%, transparent 20%);
  background-blend-mode: overlay;
  min-height: 60vh;
}

/* Animated shade sweep */
.shimmer {
  background: linear-gradient(
    90deg,
    var(--green-500),
    var(--lime-400),
    var(--green-500)
  );
  background-size: 200% 100%;
  animation: sweep 4s ease-in-out infinite;
}

@keyframes sweep {
  0%, 100% { background-position: 0% 50%; }
  50%      { background-position: 100% 50%; }
}

/* Cards: alternating shades of the same family */
.card {
  background-color: var(--green-700);
  border: 1px solid var(--lime-400);
  color: var(--lime-200);
}
.card:nth-child(even) {
  background-color: var(--green-500);
  color: var(--green-900);
}

/* Text that shifts shade on hover */
a {
  color: var(--lime-400);
  transition: color 0.3s;
}
a:hover {
  color: var(--lime-200);
}
```

**The logic behind this design:**

*   **Single Hue Family**: To keep the look harmonious, I used a lightness ramp moving from green to lime rather than using two contrasting colors.
*   **Blend Modes**: The `background-blend-mode: overlay` in the orb field allows the different shades to interact dynamically.
*   **Inverted Contrast**: By using a lime background with dark green text in the hero section, it creates a strong visual break from the dark body while staying within the same color family.
*   **Motion-Based Shading**: The shimmer effect uses an animation on the `background-position` to make the shades appear as if they are moving.

